Title: Tighten Erg.BlockedBys from []string to []Ref
Created: 2026-05-11
Author: claude-sonnet-4-6
Blocked-by: 0117

--- log ---
2026-05-11T00:00Z claude-sonnet-4-6 created

2026-05-11T00:00Z MinhHaDuong reimagined — descoped `Created → time.Time` (YAGNI: 1 read site + 1 write site, no consumer benefits from typed date, regex check is cheaper than format+parse). Scope reduced to BlockedBys only; title updated.

--- body ---
## Context
After tickets 0116 (schema-literal struct) and 0117 (validating-parser
merge), `Erg.BlockedBys` still carries raw strings that the ref grammar
can already parse. Lazy parsing via `BlockedByRefs()` is the last
surviving accessor method after 0116. Push the parse to parse-time;
delete the accessor.

## Reimagined: Created descoped
The original ticket also proposed `Created string → time.Time`. Audit
found only 1 read site (validate.go regex check) and 1 write site
(new.go string interpolation). `Created` is never compared, sorted, or
computed on — it is a display-only field. Converting saves the regex
but adds a `Format("2006-01-02")` call; net wash, plus zero-value
gotchas and import weight. Leaving `Created` as `string`.

## Proposed changes
1. `BlockedBys []string` → `BlockedBys []Ref`. Each ref is parsed at
   parse time; malformed values become errors in `parseErg`'s
   `[]string` return (per 0117). Delete `BlockedByRefs()`.
2. Update the 5 call sites that use `BlockedByRefs()` to read the typed
   field directly:
   - archive.go:63
   - check.go:48
   - close.go:129 (uses raw strings for line manipulation — preserved
     via `Ref.Raw`)
   - ready.go:243
   - validate.go: any remaining corpus-level ref users

## Out of scope
- `Created` field stays `string` (descoped — see log entry).
- Other field types stay as designed by 0116.

## Dependencies
- Hard dep: ticket 0117 (validating-parser merge). The parse-time error
  channel from 0117 is where malformed refs flow as errors.

## Exit criteria
- `Erg.BlockedBys` is `[]Ref`.
- `BlockedByRefs()` method deleted; call sites read `t.BlockedBys`
  directly.
- Malformed refs produce parse errors via 0117's mechanism.
- `make test` passes.
